e predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 56     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast with axillary tissue  30 x 23 x 9cm  a 16 x 12cm overlying skin ellipse with a ill defined  5 5cm well healed scar  and a grossly unremarkable nipple  A 3 x 2 x 2cm focally well circumscribed  round  firm solid tumor is present 8cm inferior to the nipple  0 5cm from the closest inferior inked margin  6cm from the closest deep margin  and 4cm from the closest superior inked margin  The hard  white mass is surrounded by indurated breast tissue with multiple  gritty  focally necrotic areas of breast tissue which extend approximately 3cm from the main tumor mass and extend to within 0 2cm of the superior and inferior margins   The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of fi